WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:08.487
Grow, grow, grow. That is the same
block written out three times.

2
00:00:08.707 --> 00:00:13.211
One repeat block does the same job,
and a comment says why it is there.

3
00:00:13.711 --> 00:00:18.309
A program can repeat too. The repeat
block runs the block after it.

4
00:00:18.529 --> 00:00:22.430
Repeat 3 times, jump. The cat
jumps three times in a row.

5
00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:27.247
Each time round is called an
iteration. That is three iterations.

6
00:00:27.467 --> 00:00:31.043
It repeats the one block after
it, not the whole program.

7
00:00:31.263 --> 00:00:35.489
When the count is done, the program
carries on. Say hello runs once.

8
00:00:35.989 --> 00:00:41.051
The algorithm says: go home,
move right 3 times, then grow.

9
00:00:41.271 --> 00:00:47.494
Move right 3 times is not three move
blocks. It is a repeat and a move.

10
00:00:47.714 --> 00:00:53.612
So the program is four blocks: go
home, repeat 3 times, move right, grow.

11
00:00:53.832 --> 00:00:58.430
Run it. The cat goes home, then
one square right each time round.

12
00:00:58.650 --> 00:01:03.712
Three squares, then it grows. That is
the output the algorithm asked for.

13
00:01:04.212 --> 00:01:09.041
Here is a longer program: grow,
grow, grow, wait, say hello.

14
00:01:09.261 --> 00:01:13.302
The same block three times in
a row can fold into one repeat.

15
00:01:13.522 --> 00:01:17.423
Repeat 3 times, grow.
Same output, fewer blocks.

16
00:01:17.643 --> 00:01:22.008
The wait does nothing, so it goes
as well. Five blocks become three.

17
00:01:22.228 --> 00:01:28.265
Only the same block, back to back,
folds. Jump, spin, jump cannot.

18
00:01:28.765 --> 00:01:33.409
A comment is a note beside a block.
It says what the block is for.

19
00:01:33.629 --> 00:01:37.159
It is written for people. The
computer skips it completely.

20
00:01:37.379 --> 00:01:42.301
Beside go home: reset the cat,
so every run starts the same.

21
00:01:42.521 --> 00:01:46.143
Beside the repeat: one jump
for each wall in the level.

22
00:01:46.363 --> 00:01:52.076
A comment that just says jump helps
nobody. Say why: jump over the wall.

23
00:01:52.576 --> 00:01:56.151
Next week you will have forgotten
why that wait block is there.

24
00:01:56.371 --> 00:02:00.969
The comment remembers: give the
player time to read the message.

25
00:02:01.189 --> 00:02:05.461
A partner reading your program
understands it without asking you.

26
00:02:05.681 --> 00:02:11.533
A comment says jump three times, the
block says repeat 2: a bug you have found.

27
00:02:12.033 --> 00:02:16.259
These blocks work like Scratch,
which most schools use at your age.

28
00:02:16.479 --> 00:02:20.333
Your blocks have Scratch
names. Jump is change y by 50.

29
00:02:20.553 --> 00:02:25.197
Move right is move 10 steps.
Repeat 4 times is repeat 4.

30
00:02:25.417 --> 00:02:29.318
Scratch has a comment beside any
block too, just as this does.

31
00:02:29.818 --> 00:02:35.159
A repeat block runs the one block after
it. Each time round is an iteration.

32
00:02:35.379 --> 00:02:40.348
The same block, back to back, folds
into one repeat with the same output.

33
00:02:40.568 --> 00:02:44.423
A comment is a note for people.
It says why the block is there.

34
00:02:44.643 --> 00:02:48.079
Now build a program with a
repeat in it, and comment it.
